## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: a9c1ded76ed1fc157add8ef73565bd6112967bf1

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the history of the `if (lockFoodLevel) { event.setCancelled(true); }` line in `ArenaListener.java` that the fix commit modifies, using `git log -p --follow` on the file and grepping around `lockFoodLevel` / `onFoodLevelChange`. This showed an earlier version of `onFoodLevelChange` that explicitly guarded with `!arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())` before checking `lockFoodLevel`, and a later restructuring that dropped this guard while splitting the logic into `isRunning()`/`else` branches. I confirmed with `git log -S"!arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity()))"` which pinpointed the exact commit where that check disappeared: `a9c1ded`.

**(2) Specific change:** In `a9c1ded` (2019-07-20), `onFoodLevelChange` was rewritten:
```diff
-        if (!arena.isRunning())
+        if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) {
             return;
+        }

-        if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity()))
-            return;
+        Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();

-        // If the food level is locked, cancel all changes.
-        if (lockFoodLevel)
-            event.setCancelled(true);
+        if (arena.isRunning()) {
+            if (lockFoodLevel) {
+                event.setCancelled(true);
+            }
+        } else {
+            ...
+        }
```
The old code returned early unless the player was actually `arena.inArena(p)`. The rewrite removed that guard entirely from the `isRunning()` branch, so once an arena was running, food level changes for *any* player (not just those inside the arena) were cancelled if `lockFoodLevel` was set — a regression.

**(3) Evidence:** The bug-fixing commit `5058c47` re-inserts exactly this missing condition:
```diff
-            if (lockFoodLevel) {
+            if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
```
This is a precise, minimal restoration of the guard that `a9c1ded` had dropped — the fix's `if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel)` restores the semantics of the original `!arena.inArena(...) → return` check that existed before `a9c1ded`. There is no other intervening commit touching this logic (confirmed no other match in the `-S` search besides the original 2015 introduction `0b9374d`, which predates and is unrelated to this regression). I'm confident in this identification.

